From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kristof Imeri <kristof@lanth.me>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 12:47:06 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] clutter: let a stage view filter what it shows

A shader over the whole screen could only be an offscreen effect on the
stage, which spans every monitor at one scale, paints everything again for
any damage and turns off culling.

Give a stage view a chain of fragment shaders instead. The view keeps
painting into the texture it already uses for rotated and color managed
output, so a frame still paints only what changed, and a frame where
nothing changed isn't drawn at all. The shaders run over the whole view on
each frame, and the onscreen buffer is swapped whole, since any pixel may
depend on any other. A filter that animates queues frames that run only
the shaders, without painting.

A view without a filter takes the same paths as before: no offscreen, no
extra pipeline, clipped redraws and direct scanout.

Captures paint the stage into framebuffers of their own, so they don't see
a filter, like night light. A filter can ask to be shown in them; then
they paint the whole view and filter that.

Upstream-Status: luft-only API for extension shaders
